- Follow Black code formatting
- Use isort for import sorting
- Follow PEP 8 naming conventions:
  - snake_case for functions and variables
  - PascalCase for classes
  - UPPER_CASE for constants
- Maximum line length of 120 characters
- Use absolute imports over relative imports
- Use type hints for all function parameters and returns
- Import types from `typing` module
- Use `Optional[Type]` instead of `Type | None`
- Use pytest for testing
- Create custom exception classes
- Use proper try-except blocks
- Implement proper logging
- Return proper error responses
- Handle edge cases properly
- Use proper error messages
- All unit tests are written in the tests directory
- The handlers for each function are defined in the src directory
- The handlers should only handle parsing and routing of requests. All specific logic should be handled in the methods directory
- The utilities directory contains helper functions that are shared across methods
- All data models in the backend live in the data directory and must be kept in sync with frontend data models
- The network directory contains HTTP responses that must be used by the handlers when responding
- No unit tests are needed for infrastructure code changes in the CDK
